text.section:
Any district created under this chapter may be abolished by a resolution passed by the local governing body upon the joint petition of the commission and the owners of at least 51 percent of either the land area or assessed value of land located within the district in the locality. The joint petition:

May state whether the purposes for which the district was formed substantially have been achieved;


May state that all obligations theretofore incurred by the district have been fully paid;


May describe the benefits which can be expected from the abolition of the district; and


Shall request the local governing body to abolish the district.
